+To address these limitations, this work proposes a multi-cluster boundary learning method for OOS intent detection with a cascade workflow. The workflow decouples the complex open intent detection problem into multiple simpler stages. This allows the workflow to use a lightweight MiniLM instead of LLM wih large-scale parameters. Moreover, it reduces the OOS intent detection to a one-class classification, instead of a complex multi-class classification. We investigate whether MiniLM embeddings contain useful local structure for OOS rejection. The resulting local boundaries are treated as an empirical modeling choice rather than a universally valid assumption, because additional clusters can also enlarge the acceptance region for near-OOS samples.
